{"tool_name":"tag-seq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"tag-seq","home":"https://github.com/zhoujj2013/Tag-seq","license":"MIT","summary":"A convenient and scalable method for genome-wide specificity assessment of CRISPR/Cas nucleases.","addition_date":"2021-11-17T16:19:44.876446Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-17T16:22:11.141526Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:tag-seq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"linying0216@smu.edu.cn","name":"Ying Lin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3876-5653","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"rongzhili@smu.edu.cn","name":"Zhili Rong","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1699-7074","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"zhoujj2013@smu.edu.cn","name":"Jiajian Zhou","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5206-0791","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"DNA barcoding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3200"},{"term":"Demultiplexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3933"},{"term":"Editing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3096"},{"term":"Local alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0495"},{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"}]}],"name":"Tag-seq","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S42003-021-02351-3","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Genome-wide identification of DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs) induced by CRISPR-associated protein (Cas) systems is vital for profiling the off-target events of Cas nucleases. However, current methods for off-target discovery are tedious and costly, restricting their widespread applications. Here we present an easy alternative method for CRISPR off-target detection by tracing the integrated oligonucleotide Tag using next-generation-sequencing (CRISPR-Tag-seq, or Tag-seq). Tag-seq enables rapid and convenient profiling of nuclease-induced DSBs by incorporating the optimized double-stranded oligodeoxynucleotide sequence (termed Tag), adapters, and PCR primers. Moreover, we employ a one-step procedure for library preparation in Tag-seq, which can be applied in the routine workflow of a molecular biology laboratory. We further show that Tag-seq successfully determines the cleavage specificity of SpCas9 variants and Cas12a/Cpf1 in a large-scale manner, and discover the integration sites of exogenous genes introduced by the Sleeping Beauty transposon. Our results demonstrate that Tag-seq is an efficient and scalable approach to genome-wide identification of Cas-nuclease-induced off-targets.","authors":[{"name":"Feng J."},{"name":"Hu Y."},{"name":"Huang G."},{"name":"Huang H."},{"name":"Lin Y."},{"name":"Ma S."},{"name":"Rong Z."},{"name":"Wang D."},{"name":"Zhou J."}],"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Communications Biology","title":"Tag-seq: a convenient and scalable method for genome-wide specificity assessment of CRISPR/Cas nucleases"},"pmcid":"PMC8253812","pmid":"34215845"}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Genetic engineering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3912"},{"term":"Mobile genetic elements","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0798"},{"term":"Probes and primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0632"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Tag-seq","home":"https://bio.tools/tag-seq","license":"MIT","summary":"A convenient and scalable method for genome-wide specificity assessment of CRISPR/Cas nucleases.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tag-seq/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_p